In article <1991Mar10.213318.20634@zorch.SF-Bay.ORG>, xanthian@zorch.SF-Bay.ORG (Kent Paul Dolan) writes...
>geg@beep.mis.semi.harris.com (Greg E. Garland) writes:
>> [ suggestion that polypiling drain spell casting power ]
>
>Not quite nasty enough, but here's one that is: zapping a polymorph wand
>should drain a _level_! (Even the first time, when you don't know any
>better!)
> 
>Now let people polypile all they want, but the game balance comes a little
>more back to center, or at least polypiling gets a lot less attractive.

     I doubt whether that would have much impact at all.  Currently level
drain seems to put you 1 experience point below your present level.  All
the polypiler would need to do is kill a grid bug or jackal to recover
the lost level.  Polypiling usually generates wands and scrolls of create
monster suitable for this purpose, in addition to the potions of gain level
and scrolls of genocide which unbalance the game.

     Also, it would penalize other uses of polymorph.  Zapping a wand of
polymorph at a nasty monster is a strategy which ought to be encouraged,
not discouraged, in my opinion.  Turning a mumakil into a cave spider seems
well within the spirit of the game. :-)

